# Refuses credentials, customer names and private code in public writes and pushes.
# Usage: check-public-text FILE..., --commits REV..., --tree DIR, gh-guard ARGS, or REMOTE URL.
# Reads are checked for credentials; see README.md for decisions and limitations.
#
# THE CHECK ITSELF IS public_leak_check.py, BESIDE THIS FILE. This is a launcher, and it stays at
# this name because every caller calls it: the jj shim (shims/git, the jj gate),
# shims/jj-push-hooks/pre-push, the wrapper install-prepush-hook.sh generates, and
# scripts/public-text-gate.
#
# /usr/bin/python3 -I, NEVER the python3 on PATH. This is security, not preference: PATH resolves
# through ~/.mise/shims/python3, which picks its interpreter from the CHECKOUT's tool
# configuration, and this check runs inside the repository being pushed -- so a mise shim would
# let the thing being checked choose the interpreter that checks it. `-I` also ignores
# PYTHONPATH, PYTHONHOME and the user site directory, so no module the checkout or the
# environment supplies can be imported ahead of the standard library.
#
# IF THE INTERPRETER IS MISSING OR WILL NOT START, THIS REFUSES (exit 2) and the push is blocked.
# A gate that cannot run is not a gate that passed.
